    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0741" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/394a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Second Secretary of
                        Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Nanking</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-30T14:00:00-05:00">November 30, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>368. Your 965, November 28, 9 a.m., 972, November 29, noon, and 973, November 29,
                    3 p.m.,<anchor n="60" xml:id="d807-f1"/> and Ambassador’s November 29, 4
                        p.m.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d807-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0742" n="735" xml:id="pg735"/>
                <p>The Department concurs in the Ambassador’s view that you and staff should not
                    expose yourselves to imminent and serious danger by remaining at the Embassy,
                    and feels that you and staff should remove to the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> whenever you consider it advisable to do so.
                    It is suggested that you keep in touch with your colleagues and in so far as
                    practicable concert your action with theirs.</p>
                <p>You should again urge all American citizens to evacuate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
